{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The bug was in `repo/grading.py`:\n\n```python\ndef letter_grade(score):\n    # BUG: uses > 90 so a score of exactly 90 gets a 'B'.\n    if score > 90:\n        return \"A\"\n    if score >= 80:\n        return \"B\"\n    ...\n```\n\nA score of exactly 90 failed the `> 90` check and fell through to the `>= 80` branch, returning `B`. Changed it to `>= 90` so 90 maps to `A`. Both visible tests now pass, including `test_ninety_is_A`."}]},"session_id":"53d5853c-00fb-4f70-a3c3-1e95ee871b88"}
